# Names and FAKE values only. The real file lives on the server only
# (/etc/food-orders/backend.env, mode 600) and is never committed.
# Read by compose (env_file) and passed to the backend container.
# Rules for every value: see CLAUDE.md "Staff ID and password" and "Shop and
# bank settings". Plain lines NAME=value, no `export`. Avoid `$` and ` #` in
# values (Compose reads `$` as a variable and ` #` as a comment); `openssl rand
# -hex 12` is safe. If you must use `$`, wrap the value in single quotes.

# Staff login. ID 1-64 plain printable characters; password at least 12, no
# Vietnamese accents. Make a real one with: openssl rand -hex 12
STAFF_ID=example-staff
# Deliberately too short (under 12): if you forget to replace it, the staff
# routes stay OFF (403) instead of running with a published password.
STAFF_PASSWORD=CHANGE-ME

# Optional: shop details for the summary report (all five or the report is off).
#SHOP_NAME=Example Shop
#SHOP_TAX_CODE=0000000000
#SHOP_ADDRESS=1 Example Street
#SHOP_LOCATION=1 Example Street
#SHOP_REPRESENTATIVE=Example Person

# Optional: bank transfer (all four or transfer orders answer 503).
#BANK_BIN=000000
#BANK_ACCOUNT=000000000
#BANK_ACCOUNT_NAME=EXAMPLE PERSON
#BANK_NAME=Example Bank

# Do NOT set BIND_ADDRESS, ORDERS_DB or IMAGES_DIR here: the image sets them.
